# Mixt Web OS — Apache configuration
#
# Drop this folder into your document root (htdocs/, www/, public_html/) and
# open it. Nothing else to configure.
#
# Everything the site asks for is a relative path, so it also works in a
# subdirectory:
#   http://localhost/mixt/
#
# The desktop runs with no backend at all — one local account, no mail between
# accounts, no administrator. For accounts and mail, run `npm start` and point
# Apache's /api at it; that part has to live in the virtual host, and the README
# has the snippet.
#
# If this file is ignored (some hosts set "AllowOverride None"), the site still
# works — Apache's default mime.types already knows .js and .css. These lines
# are here for the installs that do not.

# Open the desktop rather than a directory listing.
DirectoryIndex index.html

# A stylesheet served as anything other than text/css is discarded outright by
# the browser, and a script served as text/plain is refused — either one leaves
# a running OS with a white page and nothing in the document to explain it.
<IfModule mod_mime.c>
  AddType text/javascript       .js  .mjs
  AddType text/css              .css
  AddType image/svg+xml         .svg
  AddType application/json      .json
  AddType application/wasm      .wasm
</IfModule>

# Never serve a stale bundle over a changed one.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  <FilesMatch "\.(js|css)$">
    Header set Cache-Control "no-cache"
  </FilesMatch>
</IfModule>

# The bundle is ~730 kB; let Apache compress it when it can. The directive
# itself comes from mod_filter, which mod_deflate is built on, so guard on
# mod_filter — guarding on mod_deflate would test the wrong module.
<IfModule mod_filter.c>
  AddOutputFilterByType DEFLATE text/javascript text/css application/json image/svg+xml
</IfModule>

# Note: the /api proxy cannot go here. ProxyPass is registered
# RSRC_CONF|ACCESS_CONF, and AllowOverride All only grants the OR_* bits, so
# Apache rejects it in this context with "ProxyPass not allowed here" — which
# turns every request into a 500. It belongs in the virtual host; see README.
